{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: Robot-assisted surgery has become more widespread in gynecological oncology. The purpose of this systematic review is to present current knowledge on robot-assisted surgery, and to clarify and discuss controversies that have arisen alongside the development and deployment. MATERIAL AND METHODS: A database search in PubMed and EMBASE was performed up until 4 March 2016. The search strategy was developed in collaboration with an information specialist, and by application of the PRISMA guidelines. Human participants and English language were the only restrictive filters applied. Selection was performed by screening of titles and abstracts, and by full text scrutiny. From 2001 to 2016, a total of 76 references were included. RESULTS: Robot-assisted surgery in gynecological oncology has increased, and current knowledge supports that the oncological safety is similar, compared with previous surgical methods. Controversies arise because current knowledge does not clearly document the benefit of robot-assisted surgery, on perioperative outcome compared with the increased costs of the acquisition and application. CONCLUSION: The rapid development in robot-assisted surgery calls for long-term detailed prospective cohorts or randomized controlled trials. The costs associated with acquisition, application, and maintenance have an unfavorable impact on cost-benefit evaluations, especially when compared with laparoscopy. Future developments in robot-assisted surgery will hopefully lead to competition in the market, which will decrease costs.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Kristensen, Steffen E","Mosgaard, Berit J","Rosendahl, Mikkel","Dalsgaard, Tórur","Bjørn, Signe F","Frøding, Ligita P","Kehlet, Henrik","Høgdall, Claus","Lajer, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-514505"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Journal Article","Review"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"robot assisted surgery in gynecological oncology current status and controversies on patient benefits cost and surgeon conditions a systematic review","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-514505","identifier":[{"id":"28029176","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85012884164","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-cab89657-5a9c-4a9d-8ec6-ca33b889d05e"],"keyword":["Journal Article","Review"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9D348F63D4EC47A954534BE0A0AA7F07"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Surgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Steffen E","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Steffen E","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Berit J","key":"mosgaardpau","last":"Mosgaard","name":"Mosgaard, Berit J","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mikkel","key":"rosendahlpau","last":"Rosendahl","name":"Rosendahl, Mikkel","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Tórur","key":"dalsgaardpau","last":"Dalsgaard","name":"Dalsgaard, Tórur","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Signe F","key":"bjørnpau","last":"Bjørn","name":"Bjørn, Signe F","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ligita P","key":"frødingpau","last":"Frøding","name":"Frøding, Ligita P","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"kehletpau","last":"Kehlet","locid":"0a3c43a0-a0c5-4a91-85d6-6e80e16af8b5","name":"Kehlet, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-2209-1711","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Claus K","key":"høgdallpau","last":"Høgdall","locid":"c5c660ee-f61a-4d1f-a38d-7851491ce186","name":"Høgdall, Claus","name_org":"Høgdall, Claus K","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik","key":"lajerpau","last":"Lajer","name":"Lajer, Henrik","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28029176"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/aogs.13084","issn":["00016349"],"issue":"3","journal":"Acta Obstetricia et Gynecologica Scandinavica","pages":"274-285","status":"p","title":"Acta Obstetricia et Gynecologica Scandinavica","volume":"96"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85012884164"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-cab89657-5a9c-4a9d-8ec6-ca33b889d05e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Robot-assisted surgery in gynecological oncology : current status and controversies on patient benefits, cost and surgeon conditions - a systematic review","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-514505","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"This article investigates how disability can work analytically as a ‘critique from within’. Our case is the accommodation of citizens with disabilities during the voting process in Denmark. Here disability makes explicit how Danish democracy is produced as disability rubs up against implicit, normalized and mundane infrastructures and practices. We investigate disability as critique in this sense of affording a both analytic and practical ‘breakup’. To do so, we promote a ‘compositionist’ post-actor-network theory approach to disability and to polling and investigate what entry-point for critique this offers. We analyze an incident at a polling booth during the 2013 Danish Municipal election. This renders visible some of the complex socio-material processes through which citizens and the Danish state co-enact and co-authorize one another. We highlight how ‘detachments’ are vital to such processes and we examine parts of the historical background for the production of authority in the context of managing disability as exception during polling. In doing so we point out that as the organization of electoral processes evolves, new potentialities for infra-critique also emerge.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Gad, Christopher","Dalsgaard, Steffen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382456"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Compositionism","Detachment","Disability","Elections","Infra critique"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"disability as infra critique a compositionist approach to the election process in denmark","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81976799/Disability_as_infra_critique_a_compositionist_approach_to_the_election_process_in_Denmark_preprint_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382456","identifier":[{"id":"85019129765","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-4f5511f1-001d-4c84-a292-8062ea821a18"],"keyword":["Disability","compositionism","detachment","elections","infra-critique"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C94D7D73E61D9D0D0517D47D46042D2C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81976799/Disability_as_infra_critique_a_compositionist_approach_to_the_election_process_in_Denmark_preprint_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice","The Department, TiP and Games Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christopher","key":"gadpau","last":"Gad","locid":"d55dab65-fffe-4da4-a383-cfcf5ee3a8cd","name":"Gad, Christopher","orcid":"0000-0002-1631-5483","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Steffen","key":"dalsgaardpau","last":"Dalsgaard","locid":"bc7a60f7-45a0-401f-813f-6b4aa700c849","name":"Dalsgaard, Steffen","orcid":"0000-0003-3712-6988","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/17530350.2017.1312485","issn":["17530350","17530369"],"issn_org":["17530350"],"issue":"3","journal":"Journal of Cultural Economy","pages":"237-250","publisher":"Routledge","status":"p","title":"Journal of Cultural Economy","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85019129765"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-4f5511f1-001d-4c84-a292-8062ea821a18"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Disability as infra-critique : A compositionist approach to the election process in Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382456","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"This article discusses how a small place – the polling booth – can be bounded as an ethnographic site with reference to the political and democratic event that it is supposed to facilitate. Concerns about the socio-material bounding of the booth form the main empirical case – a debate, which recently occurred in Denmark when the government proposed to digitalise voting. Digitalisation here became a controversy because of the potential illicit influences that computer experts argued would enter the polling booth and challenge the secrecy and the privacy of the vote, the transparency of the electoral process, and thus the electoral enactment of democracy itself. In this way the polling booth potentially works as an ethnographic entry point for following shifts in contemporary debates","author_count":2,"contributors":["Dalsgaard, Steffen","Gad, Christopher"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384053"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Democracy","Digitalisation","Elections","Ethnography","Event","Place"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"digital unbounding of the polling booth ethnography in small places","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82086505/Dalsgaard_Gad_2017_Digital_polling_booth.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384053","identifier":[{"id":"85021924924","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-be163cd2-c2c6-495e-98b8-ba5398418323"],"keyword":["democracy","digitalisation","elections","ethnography","event","place"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5910500867ACEBBDCE938F78A06ED11E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","u