{"abstract":"This article refers to carbon valuation as the practice of ascribing value to, and assessing the value of, actions and objects in terms of carbon emissions. Due to the pervasiveness of carbon emissions in the actions and objects of everyday lives of human beings, the making of carbon offsets and credits offers almost unlimited repertoires of alternatives to be included in contemporary carbonvaluation schemes. Consequently, the article unpacks how discussions of carbon valuation are interpreted through different registers of alternatives—as the ommensuration and substitution of variants on the one hand, and the confrontational comparison of radical difference on the other. Through the reading of a wide selection of the social science literature on carbon markets and trading, the article argues that the value of carbon emissions itself depends on the construction of alternative, hypothetical scenarios, and that emissions have become both a moral and a virtual measure pitting diverse forms of actualised actions or objects against each other or against corresponding nonactions and non-objects as alternatives.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Dalsgaard, Steffen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383888"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Carbon credits","Climate change","Commensuration","Market","Value","alternative"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"carbon valuation alternatives alternations and lateral measures","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3384/VS.2001-5992.164167","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383888","ids":["itu-b3fce2d9-93d5-4108-ac2f-04fd5d1f4655"],"keyword":["alternative","carbon credits","climate change","commensuration","market","value"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-7412CC7193AE5CF11CCF874C25199B64"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82354719/VS.2001_5592.164167.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3384/VS.2001-5992.164167","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice","The Department, TiP and Games Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Steffen","key":"dalsgaardpau","last":"Dalsgaard","locid":"bc7a60f7-45a0-401f-813f-6b4aa700c849","name":"Dalsgaard, Steffen","orcid":"0000-0003-3712-6988","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3384/vs.2001-5992.164167","issn":["20015992"],"issue":"1","journal":"Valuation Studies","pages":"67-91","publisher":"Linköping University Press","status":"p","title":"Valuation Studies","volume":"4"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b3fce2d9-93d5-4108-ac2f-04fd5d1f4655"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Carbon Valuation: Alternatives, Alternations and Lateral Measures?","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383888","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"New social media have become indispensable to people all over the world as platforms for communication, with Facebook being the most popular. Hence, platforms such as Facebook are also becoming crucial tools for ethnographers because much social life now exists ‘online’. What types of field relations stem from such social media-driven ethnography? And what kinds of data do these relations present to the ethnographer? These questions must be considered in order to understand the challenges Facebook and other social media pose to ethnographic methodology. This article focuses on how Facebook may play an important role even in ethnographic work concerned with questions other than how Facebook works as a social medium. Most importantly it allows the ethnographer to keep up-to-date with the field. I argue that ethnography is already in possession of the methodological tools critically to assess the validity and value of data gathered or produced via Facebook including issues such as authenticity which are also pertinent to digital ethnography.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Dalsgaard, Steffen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384161"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Ethnography","Facebook","Fieldwork","Papua New Guinea","Social media"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the ethnographic use of facebook in everyday life","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82419657/Dalsgaard_2016_Ethnographic_Use_of_Facebook_final.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384161","identifier":[{"id":"84961775115","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-c51d3824-cd74-4f63-8901-ce98b4e1cd69"],"keyword":["Ethnography","Facebook","Fieldwork","Papua New Guinea","Social media"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4E904404234524A8E1391AD249D6CADD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82419657/Dalsgaard_2016_Ethnographic_Use_of_Facebook_final.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice","The Department, Interdisciplinary Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Steffen","key":"dalsgaardpau","last":"Dalsgaard","locid":"bc7a60f7-45a0-401f-813f-6b4aa700c849","name":"Dalsgaard, Steffen","orcid":"0000-0003-3712-6988","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/00664677.2016.1148011","issn":["00664677","14692902"],"issn_org":["00664677"],"issue":"1","journal":"Anthropological Forum - A Journal of Social Anthropology and Comparative Sociology","pages":"96-114","publisher":"Routledge","status":"p","title":"Anthropological Forum - A Journal of Social Anthropology and Comparative Sociology","volume":"26"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84961775115"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-c51d3824-cd74-4f63-8901-ce98b4e1cd69"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Ethnographic Use of Facebook in Everyday Life","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384161","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
