{"abstract":"The adoption of the Kyoto Protocol was a major breakthrough in committing industrialized countries to reduce their emissions of greenhouse gases, even if the effect is disputed. The protocol works through mechanisms that ascribe value to the environment in terms of those emissions—a numerical value based on carbon, which is then translated into a monetary value. This article reviews the different understandings of value implicated in debates about the environment seen through carbon. It does this by contrasting the values embedded in some of the various initiatives that have resulted from the Kyoto Protocol, and how they relate to the market, government control, and individual consumer morality, among other things. Controversy over carbon trading is entangled in the capacity of carbon to commensurate a wide range of human and non-human actions via their cost in emissions, which nevertheless is countered by moral differentiation.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Dalsgaard, Steffen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384175"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Carbon","Consumption","Development","Economy","Market","Morality","Value","commensurability"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"carbon value between equivalence and differentiation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-384175","ids":["itu-c6387b2b-35c2-4197-99c5-80ff99545dad"],"keyword":["carbon","commensurability","consumption","development","economy","market","morality","value"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-3426BF4C2DE2DD0CEE4DBC0326FEE604"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice","The Department, Interdisciplinary Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Steffen","key":"dalsgaardpau","last":"Dalsgaard","locid":"bc7a60f7-45a0-401f-813f-6b4aa700c849","name":"Dalsgaard, Steffen","orcid":"0000-0003-3712-6988","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["21506779","21506787"],"issn_org":["21506779"],"journal":"Environment and Society","pages":"86-102","publisher":"Berghahn Books","status":"p","title":"Environment and Society","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-c6387b2b-35c2-4197-99c5-80ff99545dad"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Carbon Value between Equivalence and Differentiation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384175","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Udspillet fra regeringen om dimensionering af universiteternes uddannelser eksemplificerer på dramatisk vis, hvordan politisk styring fratager universiteterne muligheden for strategisk planlægning. Forskervejen vil blive mindre attraktiv.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Gerken, Mikkel","Bille, Mikkel","Dalsgaard, Steffen","Haugbolle, Sune","Lindorff-Larsen, Kresten","Sylvest, Casper","Søgaard, Anders","Veel, Kristin"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-038381"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"pop","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"forskningen er i fare kommentar","src":["itu","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dna","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.b.dk/kommentarer/forskningen-er-i-fare","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-038381","ids":["itu-cb646eb2-a0d5-43e1-8297-0d0d16891691","ruc-dcc9b6a7-088e-4339-9453-2014008d7ee1"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-2-BA8AE358A1A3E3E77361B14C62F99FDC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.b.dk/kommentarer/forskningen-er-i-fare","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, Space, Place, Mobility and Urban Studies","Roskilde University, The Department of Environmental, Social and Spatial Change"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copen