{"abstract":"The introduction of the Kyoto Protocol is an attempt to save the climate through a number of schemes, or mechanisms, that commodify carbon. Among other things, these schemes create monetary incentives to reduce carbon emissions through the trade of permits and credits, and they make carbon an object of financial speculation. Most controversial is apparently the potential of carbon thus to be a universal yardstick for value by commensurating moral spheres of human action (the environment, the economy, development, etc.) that some people regard as distinct. This paper explores the consequences of the speculative aspects of carbon as a standard of value and as potential currency.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Dalsgaard, Steffen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381784"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Carbon","Commodification","Economy","Environment","Value","commensurability"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the commensurability of carbon making value and money on climate change","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84901463873","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381784","identifier":[{"id":"84901463873","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-22785fdb-6e18-4afe-a5b4-e36ef44b5eea"],"keyword":["carbon","commensurability","commodification","economy","environment","value"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-5A00CF14CDC9A8AB8A537A1A7F242F0F"],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice","The Department, Culture, Aesthetics, Organisations and Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Steffen","key":"dalsgaardpau","last":"Dalsgaard","locid":"bc7a60f7-45a0-401f-813f-6b4aa700c849","name":"Dalsgaard, Steffen","orcid":"0000-0003-3712-6988","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["20491115"],"issue":"1","journal":"HAU: Journal of Ethnographic Theory","pages":"80-98","publisher":"University of Chicago Press","status":"p","title":"HAU: Journal of Ethnographic Theory","volume":"3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-22785fdb-6e18-4afe-a5b4-e36ef44b5eea"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Commensurability of Carbon: Making Value and Money on Climate Change","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381784","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Digitalizing electoral processes entails substantial changes to the materialities on which such processes rely, and hence to how they are practiced, organized, and, in turn, how they may be analyzed and reflected upon. As researchers in the Danish strategic research project DemTech, which investigates whether it is possible to ‘modernize’ the Danish electoral process without jeopardizing the trust of the voters, we have met a multitude of ideas about the present and future ways of doing elections in Denmark, e.g. their perceived advantages and disadvantages. In this paper based on ethnographic work-in-progress we will focus on one particular ‘problem’ which emerges in light of the project and the current efforts to digitalize electoral processes. That is, the problem of how a vote is constituted and defined as such; how the ways in which a vote works are related to its (potential) material/technological manifestations, and how it is handled, processed, counted and accounted for. In other words we will discuss, drawing on current STS and anthropological approaches to ontology, technology, politics and democracy, what it takes for a vote to become a vote, what it means that a vote is both a product and producer of 'the state', ‘citizenship' and ‘democracy’, and what it means if a vote cannot be defined as one exact ‘thing’, but instead may, simultaneously, be many things at once.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Dalsgaard, Steffen","Gad, Christopher"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383055"],"event":{"end":"2013-10-12","place":"San Diego, us","start":"2013-10-09","title":"Society for Social Studies of Science","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Digitalization of electoral processes","Electoral materialities","STS and anthropological approaches to democracy","Technological manifestations in voting","Voter trust"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"what makes a vote and what does a vote make","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://citation.allacademic.com/meta/p_mla_apa_research_citation/6/6/4/8/9/p664895_index.html#association","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383055","ids":["itu-797d4e6e-ee81-4af7-9bef-754554b48187"],"keyword":["Digitalization of electoral processes","Electoral materialities","STS and anthropological approaches to democracy","Technological manifestations in voting","Voter trust"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-35920775602F941B3B59F1195FEC3021"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://citation.allacademic.com/meta/p_mla_apa_research_citation/6/6/4/8/9/p664895_index.html#association","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice","The Department, IT management and leadership"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Steffen","key":"dalsgaardpau","last":"Dalsgaard","locid":"bc7a60f7-45a0-401f-813f-6b4aa700c849","name":"Dalsgaard, Steffen","orcid":"0000-0003-3712-6988","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christopher","key":"gadpau","last":"Gad","locid":"d55dab65-fffe-4da4-a383-cfcf5ee3a8cd","name":"Gad, Christopher","orcid":"0000-0002-1631-5483","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-797d4e6e-ee81-4af7-9bef-754554b48187"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"What makes a vote, and what does a vote make?","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383055","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
