Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9781781905418"],"pages":"277-302","publisher":"Emerald Group Publishing","status":"p","title":"Engaging with Capitalism: Cases from Oceania"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84886856374"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-6f71042c-2cf9-46e9-baa2-a5dc3122840e"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Politics of Remittance and the Role of Returning Migrants: Localizing Capitalism in Manus Province, Papua New Guinea","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382927","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"The future for REDD+ in Papua New Guinea (PNG) seems uncertain in these days. Logging companies are accessing much land via a controversial legal framework (Special Agricultural Business Lease), while conservation-oriented NGOs are struggling to find schemes to stop the deforestation. After the failure of voluntary carbon trade due largely to scams, REDD+ has been their new darling. However, there are currently only a few pilot projects mainly in areas, without large-scale logging. This paper argues that to understand the possibility for successfully implementing REDD+, one must look at the development of the forestry sector as a whole with its competing actors, technologies and forms of social organisation. The challenges to conservation come not only from 'above' (logging industry and policy-makers) and from 'below' (poverty and complex customary land tenure), but also from the union of these two levels. While the portable sawmill is not new in PNG, it is only recently that logging companies have begun to sponsor small-scale community logging, which otherwise is considered more sustainable than industrial logging. This decentralisation of the logging industry to a 'participatory mode', where landowners log their own trees may paradoxically be the biggest challenge to conservation in PNG rather than its last hope.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Dalsgaard, Steffen","Pedersen, Marianne"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383132"],"event":{"end":"2013-07-05","place":"Lissabon, pt","start":"2013-07-02","title":"EuroSEAS","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Conservation policy","Deforestation","Logging","Papua New Guinea","REDD"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the portable sawmill and other challenges to redd in papua new guinea","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.mgimo.ru/files2/y07_2013/240728/Proceedings%20final-dia26(1).pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383132","ids":["itu-7f7b497a-ab76-4a85-bdfe-9d5815f59235"],"keyword":["Conservation Policy","Deforestation","Logging","Papua New Guinea","REDD+"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-314C2ABDF4FE54CA61FFA68982EEE960"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.mgimo.ru/files2/y07_2013/240728/Proceedings%20final-dia26(1).pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice","The Department, IT management and leadership"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Steffen","key":"dalsgaardpau","last":"Dalsgaard","locid":"bc7a60f7-45a0-401f-813f-6b4aa700c849","name":"Dalsgaard, Steffen","orcid":"0000-0003-3712-6988","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Marianne","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Marianne","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-7f7b497a-ab76-4a85-bdfe-9d5815f59235"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Portable Sawmill and Other Challenges to REDD+ in Papua New Guinea","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383132","year":"2013","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"In sociological literature, the most commonly accepted meaning of 'the state' is based on a spatial definition that describes it as an entity exercising sovereignty within a bounded territory. However, the state is also made present in time, and state forms have a profound impact on the temporalities of social events and interaction, for instance, through rhythms and schedules. Consequently, this article discusses how the state in Manus Province, Papua New Guinea, can be understood with reference to temporality as much as to spatiality and materiality. Here, the state is seen as being personified in its politicians, who are in control of its resources. In this understanding, the state is both facilitated and limited by the presence, attention, and duration of the politicians, who are obliged to recognize personal relationships through which kin or acquaintances can challenge bureaucratic control of space and of time.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Dalsgaard, Steffen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384642"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Fieldwork","Materiality","Papua New Guinea","Social interaction","Space","State","Temporality","Time"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the time of the state and the temporality of the gavman in manus province papua new guinea","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-384642","ids":["itu-e53cb743-cb65-4314-a212-dbae8e407d18"],"keyword":["Papua New Guinea","fieldwork","materiality","social interaction","space","state","temporality","time"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-2AE2660391AE497E6EC771882B17A6E9"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice","The Department, Culture, Aesthetics, Organisations and Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Steffen","key":"dalsgaardpau","last":"Dalsgaard","locid":"bc7a60f7-45a0-401f-813f-6b4aa700c849","name":"Dalsgaard, Steffen","orcid":"0000-0003-3712-6988","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["0155977X","15585727"],"issn_org":["0155977X"],"issue":"1","journal":"Social Analysis: The International Journal of Anthropology","pages":"34-49","publisher":"Berghahn Books","status":"p","title":"Social Analysis: The International Journal of Anthropology","volume":"57"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e53cb743-cb65-4314-a212-dbae8e407d18"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Time of the State and the Temporality of the Gavman in Manus Province, Papua New Guinea","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384642","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"We present the detection of five planets - Kepler-62b, c, d, e, and f - of size 1.31, 0.54, 1.95, 1.61 and 1.41 Earth radii (R), orbiting a K2V star at periods of 5.7, 12.4, 18.2, 122.4, and 267.3 days, respectively. The outermost planets, Kepler-62e and -62f, are super-Earth-size (1.25 R <planet radius ≤ 2.0 R) planets in the habitable zone of their host star, respectively receiving 1.2 ± 0.2 times and 0.41 ± 0.05 times the solar flux at Earth's orbit. Theoretical models of Kepler-62e and -62f for a stellar age of ∼7 billion years suggest that both planets could be solid, either with a rocky composition or composed of mostly solid water in their bulk.","author_count":67,"contributors":["Borucki, W.J.","Agol, E.","Fressin, F.","Kaltenegger, L.","Rowe, J.","Isaacson, H.","Fischer, D.","Batalha, N.","Lissauer, J.J.","Marcy, G.W.","Fabrycky, D.","Désert, J.-M.","Bryson, S.T.","Barclay, Thomas","Bastien, F.","Boss, A.","Brugamyer, E.","Buchhave, L.A.","Burke, C.","Caldwell, D.A.","Carter, J.","Charbonneau, D.","Crepp, J.R.","Christensen-Dalsgaard, Jørgen","Christiansen, J.L.","Ciardi, D.","Cochran, W.D.","DeVore, E.","Doyle, L.","Dupree, A.K.","Endl, M.","Everett, M.E.","Ford, E.B.","Fortney, J.","Gautier III, T.N.","Geary, J.C.","Gould, A.","Haas, M.","Henze, C.","Howard, A.W.","Howell, S.B.","Huber, D.","Jenkins, J.M.","Kjeldsen, Hans","Kolbl, R.","Kolodziejczak, J.","Latham, D.W.","Lee, Brian L.","Lopez, E.","Mullally, F.","Orosz, J.A.","Prsa, A.","Quintana, E.V.","Sanchis-Ojeda, R.","Sasselov, D.","Seader, S.","Shporer, A.","Steffen, J.H.","Still, Martin","Tenenbaum, P.","Thompson, S.E.","Torres, G.","Twicken, J.D.","Welsh, W.F.","Winn, J.N."],"cuid":["S02-099.46-030321"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ames Research Center","California Institute of Technology",